## Complementary filter

On CC3D hardware, a simple complementary filter fuses the accelerometer and gyroscope to estimate attitude (orientation).  
Limitations:

- Skewed by centripetal/long-duration turning forces (e.g., flying in circles).
- Cannot compute speed or position.
- Cannot estimate yaw/heading without a magnetometer (CC3D has no compass).

---

## State estimation with Extended Kalman Filter (EKF)

Typical flight-controller sensors cannot directly observe the full system state (position, velocity, attitude). Instead, they measure:

- Inertial quantities: rotation (gyros) and acceleration (accelerometers),  
- Heading: magnetometer,  
- Altitude: barometer,  
- Global position and ground speed: GPS.

These measurements are **noisy**, **inaccurate**, and **temperature-dependent**, so a sensor-fusion filter (EKF) is used to produce a consistent state estimate.

---

## State

Revolution-class boards run an EKF that estimates a **13-dimensional** state with full covariance in real time:

| # | State Variable |
|---|----------------|
| 1 | Position **N** (North) |
| 2 | Position **E** (East) |
| 3 | Position **D** (Down) |
| 4 | Velocity **N** |
| 5 | Velocity **E** |
| 6 | Velocity **D** |
| 7 | Quaternion **Q0** |
| 8 | Quaternion **Q1** |
| 9 | Quaternion **Q2** |
| 10 | Quaternion **Q3** |
| 11 | Gyro bias **X** |
| 12 | Gyro bias **Y** |
| 13 | Gyro bias **Z** |

